Root cause:
The bug was caused by an uninitialized variable `wd_reg_val` and an array index overrun when the loop variable `i` reached the size of the `bq25980_watchdog_time` array. Specifically, the original code did not properly handle the case where `bq->watchdog_timer` was equal to or greater than the maximum value in the `bq25980_watchdog_time` array, leading to an attempt to access an out-of-bounds index (`i + 1`), which could result in undefined behavior. The patch initializes `wd_reg_val` to a default value and adds a check to ensure that the loop does not exceed the valid index range of the array.
